[{:db/id "q-86608/selection/85e8925e9dab7a7a3b098a81c707a459cbee9f7efb7f26996b720ae264f7f6bc" :answer/id #uuid "07ff1a0c-8c51-5b6c-aa75-cb4b76ff5e6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86608/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c40e5907-388b-5096-b456-eb41edc615d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86608/selection/7b1adac05d0322c1b077c09ab60ccc310f2fd8b506947a180cce3b840f96d2f5" :answer/id #uuid "43284900-457c-56ce-9bc6-8ab74bef0ad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5+5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86608/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "e8ad4f28-97c0-5e99-b5f2-5d8b3ad46e3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86608/selection/3ed651463d357ca79e32c9263b6e2b4c673dda53b752516d9fb3f9f6965cd470" :answer/id #uuid "d3817dea-427e-5e53-bd52-90c48de3ed02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5+5\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86608/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c92f4f53-f1f5-5d69-91f7-84a5925be615" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86608/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-86608/selection/85e8925e9dab7a7a3b098a81c707a459cbee9f7efb7f26996b720ae264f7f6bc" "q-86608/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-86608/selection/7b1adac05d0322c1b077c09ab60ccc310f2fd8b506947a180cce3b840f96d2f5" "q-86608/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-86608/selection/3ed651463d357ca79e32c9263b6e2b4c673dda53b752516d9fb3f9f6965cd470"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86608" :question/id #uuid "27867e5f-503f-55f0-90fd-c63c9bbf31c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-86608" :question/problem "Express $z=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))$ in the form $z=x+\\text{i}y.$" :question/worked-solution "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =5(-1+\\text{i}\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-86608/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86608"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" :answer/id #uuid "0343d9f1-8adc-5264-8457-700aa44c4475" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478/selection/a4d7e4f3c2d8bf3cf6c6f70a47ff3bed48296fb7e830bcbd9b0fbcc86487899b" :answer/id #uuid "7ca20a91-0055-535e-bc15-9afa3af1e2e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478/selection/d663f1168c4681f7aa14f4c923c3b72043d9b118c001cc3f782a5b1d9555b3f2" :answer/id #uuid "4f77f758-81fb-5b97-9247-65c5dabac5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478/selection/06b8e4c4bcae4b444d1035cdcce9d2ae75d49134f9cb952dab19cd2db5e27306" :answer/id #uuid "a3ab40e4-681d-5fb5-a137-e0d3f1769ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478/selection/544593eb60675094893973e52c3829e2727eeeb65f2f436a012fe3dafb22bbb4" :answer/id #uuid "acf51d53-ebcf-50fc-9117-ce6f5d3dabaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e16ee0ba-b5a8-5f88-8376-d08aee32e493" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107478/selection/d663f1168c4681f7aa14f4c923c3b72043d9b118c001cc3f782a5b1d9555b3f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-107478/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" "q-107478/selection/a4d7e4f3c2d8bf3cf6c6f70a47ff3bed48296fb7e830bcbd9b0fbcc86487899b" "q-107478/selection/d663f1168c4681f7aa14f4c923c3b72043d9b118c001cc3f782a5b1d9555b3f2" "q-107478/selection/06b8e4c4bcae4b444d1035cdcce9d2ae75d49134f9cb952dab19cd2db5e27306" "q-107478/selection/544593eb60675094893973e52c3829e2727eeeb65f2f436a012fe3dafb22bbb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107478" :question/id #uuid "663d89fa-6933-5875-9f60-94f2abd7d111" :question/math-academy-id "q-107478" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{4}{1-\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1+\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{4}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{1+1} \\\\  & =2(1+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=2+2\\text{i},$ the magnitude is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=2$ and $y=2$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107478/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107478"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550/selection/cec3927ed937a9d8279acce734fd6c8b6542e1d2516f1f70a33c267906e827cd" :answer/id #uuid "7a66290d-b014-5aba-87d1-a858e8bd306e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550/selection/1c82a071529a2be03e82681c67cf2d3a94bfd2d6b29db5826bb2c9f4e877597f" :answer/id #uuid "e56afc50-f55b-59a0-8b5c-f99d8ff7ade3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" :answer/id #uuid "56ee7ebe-98fd-5a33-bee4-535eeb797b9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550/selection/bbd431f5091401b486ce5fbe2841ae3adf1cdcb75003491fc9d19d831ddfc917" :answer/id #uuid "94366a7b-6797-5da8-96b7-252988ed66ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550/selection/a4d7e4f3c2d8bf3cf6c6f70a47ff3bed48296fb7e830bcbd9b0fbcc86487899b" :answer/id #uuid "da2ef5f6-f7af-550f-94f1-33b120c84acf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "09d9464c-98e9-5d2d-964c-3d811c212b40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107550/selection/a4d7e4f3c2d8bf3cf6c6f70a47ff3bed48296fb7e830bcbd9b0fbcc86487899b" :answer-field/choices ["q-107550/selection/cec3927ed937a9d8279acce734fd6c8b6542e1d2516f1f70a33c267906e827cd" "q-107550/selection/1c82a071529a2be03e82681c67cf2d3a94bfd2d6b29db5826bb2c9f4e877597f" "q-107550/selection/17853c29bb5a9ae967d170884b153a9eb8695abb03566f991fd5c66dafd8808f" "q-107550/selection/bbd431f5091401b486ce5fbe2841ae3adf1cdcb75003491fc9d19d831ddfc917" "q-107550/selection/a4d7e4f3c2d8bf3cf6c6f70a47ff3bed48296fb7e830bcbd9b0fbcc86487899b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107550" :question/id #uuid "f613da52-505f-5404-adc3-5208cbe64ea2" :question/math-academy-id "q-107550" :question/problem "Express $z=\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1-\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}(1-\\text{i})}{(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}-2{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}+2}{1+1} \\\\  & =1+\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=1+\\text{i},$ the magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=1$ and $y=1$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107550/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d1ea5c4-2700-5c03-a22e-de5439f47c36"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107550"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107567/selection/4ffcda1a94c739fb47233023be296bd90820c1b0cae8d79aa47128d530346d88" :answer/id #uuid "05924717-2a38-5c3d-98d3-5a905885ec0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107567/selection/ac1bc2791841924ad1bc003380c7b4964336f2426612db6bd02828d9c2814658" :answer/id #u