ince $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )) \\\\  & =2(-1+\\text{i}\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107567/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-324344/field-1/b5348ddf71e5472e38f3abfd1fd508b6086b48d4f20aefdbfcdf24c25a3eb0ab" :answer/id #uuid "11173924-f470-535e-af7a-a9d22f50b7b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324344/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6d755c0-7f14-54a5-bbcc-e613bc2ec08d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-324344/field-1/b5348ddf71e5472e38f3abfd1fd508b6086b48d4f20aefdbfcdf24c25a3eb0ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-324344/field-1/b5348ddf71e5472e38f3abfd1fd508b6086b48d4f20aefdbfcdf24c25a3eb0ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-324344/field-2/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer/id #uuid "a5597b49-a9aa-52b2-9160-dd4714df2f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324344/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "57d82154-7d5b-5c7f-8c4f-5fd4bbe14d9e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-324344/field-2/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-324344/field-2/219833e72de92bafe4f4f5813822a337104a6b771fd9bf741ddcca8750ecab9e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-324344" :question/id #uuid "23ea12f8-9a24-5e0b-91e4-c1511d048c42" :question/math-academy-id "q-324344" :question/problem "Express $z=8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}))$ in the form $z=x+y\\,\\text{i},$ where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Give the **exact** values of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-$\n{{field-2}}\n$i$" :question/worked-solution "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nFirst, we find $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the values and expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =8(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\text{i}\\,(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{2}-4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-324344/field-1" "q-324344/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31e4455a-9f8f-5c12-8c96-bb6735691591"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-324344"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
